{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Gm]During his reign the king of [Eb]Babylon invaded
[Gm]Jehoiakim served him for three [F]years
[Gm]Then he turned and rebelled a[Eb]gainst the master
The [Gm]LORD sent raiding bands against the [F]land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ne[Bb]buchadnezzar king of Baby[F]lon my servant
[Gm]I will bring them against this [Eb]land
To de[Bb]vote them to de[F]struction
An object of horror and [Gm]scorn
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
All who see you will re[Eb]coil from you
[Gm]And if it's ruined, who will [F]mourn?
Are [Gm]you better than Thebes seated by the [Eb]Nile
Yet she [Gm]too went into ex[F]ile
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]This whole land will become a ru[Bb]in
[F]A wasteland for seventy [Gm]years [Gm7/F]
[Eb]The sound of joy will be ban[Bb]ished
From the [F]city and the fields
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will [Bb]punish the king of [F]Babylon
[Gm]And that nation for their [Eb]guilt
The [Bb]land of Chaldeans made [F]a desola[Gm]tion
{end_of_verse}

